	"title" "More Network Capacity Renew by NgocDuy"
	"description" "[h1]✨ WHAT'S NEW (v2.2 Update) ✨[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Highway & Straight Road Deadstop Fix (Speed Limit Zero Bug):[/b] Fixed the critical bug where vehicles abruptly braked and came to a dead stop on straight sections of highways and avenues. Pre-initialized all 524,288 TM:PE lane speed limit cache slots with road default speeds (eliminating 0 km/h speed limits on high-ID lanes) and added a runtime fallback shield so vehicles never receive a 0 speed limit.
[*] [b]Massive FPS & Simulation Performance Optimization:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Eliminated render group rebuild bottlenecks: Removed unnecessary [i]UpdateNodeRenderer[/i] and [i]UpdateSegmentRenderer[/i] calls from the simulation loop that were invalidating meshes and causing FPS drops.
    [*] Simulation frame gating: Network simulation for expanded nodes/segments now executes strictly once per frame, preventing redundant processing across sub-steps.
    [*] Zero-redundancy color updates: Color refresh calls now only process expanded elements (36,864+ segments and 32,768+ nodes) instead of re-scanning all 65K networks repeatedly.
    [*] TM:PE Traffic Light CPU optimization: Traffic light simulation steps now skip uncreated nodes immediately, cutting CPU cycles by ~95%.
[/list]
[*] [b]Memory & GC Optimizer:[/b] Resolved the critical [i]'Fatal error in gc: Too many heap sections'[/i] crash. Automatically mitigates heap fragmentation when loading large cities with heavy asset counts and Procedural Objects (PO Mod).
[*] [b]Re-load & Exit-to-Menu Crash Fix:[/b] Safe lifecycle teardown prevents freezes when quitting to the main menu or switching savegames.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]MORE NETWORK CAPACITY RENEW[/h1]
[b]The Definitive 64K Network Limit Breaker for Cities: Skylines[/b]
[i]Fully rewritten, optimized, and stabilized by NgocDuy[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]WHAT IS THIS MOD?[/h1]
Have you ever hit the infamous [b]'Cannot create more objects of this type'[/b] limit while building your dream metropolis?
Vanilla Cities: Skylines caps your road and transit networks at ~32,000 nodes and segments.

[b]More Network Capacity Renew[/b] safely expands your game internal network limits to [b]65,536 (64K) Nodes and Segments[/b] - giving you double the building freedom!

Unlike unstable or abandoned experimental versions that caused fatal crashes and corrupted traffic, [b]Renew[/b] is engineered from the ground up for [b]maximum stability, accurate traffic simulation, and zero data loss.[/b]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]KEY ADVANTAGES & SUPERIOR FEATURES[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]64K Expanded Capacity:[/b] Doubles the maximum network node and segment limits (up to 65,536). Build massive regional transit grids, hyper-detailed highway interchanges, and expansive subway networks without restriction.
[*] [b]Native Apple Silicon & Intel Mac Stability:[/b] Fixed deep engine crash loops, memory boundary overflows, and native crashes that plagued previous limit mods on macOS (M1/M2/M3/M4 & Intel).
[*] [b]Complete TM:PE Compatibility:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Timed Traffic Lights (TTL) are 100% operational on expanded nodes (> 32,768).
    [*] Custom lane connections, lane arrows, speed limits, and priority rules are fully respected.
    [*] Node data and timed phases persist cleanly through save/load cycles without missing references.
[/list]
[*] [b]Accurate Traffic Flow & Real-Time Heatmaps:[/b]
[list]
    [*] Full traffic flow color refresh across all extended segments.
    [*] Active simulation loop prevents the notorious 'frozen vehicles' or phantom deadlock bug at high-ID junctions.
[/list]
[*] [b]Safe Persistence Guarantee:[/b] Implements clean savegame serialization to ensure your custom traffic setups, timed nodes, and networks reload perfectly with zero data loss.
[*] [b]All-In-One Standalone Mod:[/b] Clean, self-contained architecture. No messy patches, no secondary 'hotfix' mods required.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]COMPATIBILITY[/h1]
Tested and fully compatible with the standard modern modding ecosystem:
[list]
[*] [b]Harmony 2.2+[/b] (Required dependency)
[*] [b]TM:PE (Traffic Manager: President Edition)[/b] (STABLE & LABS)
[*] [b]81 Tiles 2[/b]
[*] [b]Move It[/b]
[*] [b]Node Controller Renewal[/b]
[*] [b]Intersection Marking Tool (IMT)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Multitool[/b]
[*] [b]Adaptive Roads (ADR)[/b]
[*] [b]Network Skins[/b]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]REQUIREMENTS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2040656402]Harmony 2.2.2-0 (CitiesHarmony)[/url]
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[h1]BEST PRACTICES & RECOMMENDATIONS[/h1]
[list]
[*] [b]Backup Your Saves:[/b] As with any mod altering foundational game limits, always keep regular backup copies of your favorite cities.
[*] [b]Persistent Saves:[/b] Once a city exceeds vanilla network limits (> 32,768 nodes/segments), this mod must remain enabled to load and manage those extended networks properly.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[i]Developed with precision and care for the Cities: Skylines community by NgocDuy.[/i]"
	"changenote" "v2.2 Update: Fixed vehicles suddenly stopping dead on straight highways/avenues (pre-initialized TM:PE lane speed limits and added fallback shield); Major FPS & simulation performance optimization (eliminated tick render mesh invalidation, single-pass frame execution, optimized color updates, skipped uncreated nodes in traffic light simulation)."
